<LegalLayout title="Support - Back Pain Log" description="Support and help for the Back Pain Log iOS app.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Back Pain Log</p>
  <h1>Support</h1>

  <p>Back Pain Log is a calm, private lower-back discomfort diary for iPhone and iPad. It helps you save a daily discomfort score, note treatments, review simple trends, and export a CSV if you want to share your history with a physio, GP, or your own records.</p>

  <h2>Common questions</h2>

  <h2>Where is my data stored?</h2>
  <p>Your data is stored locally on your device. Back Pain Log has no account system and no cloud sync.</p>

  <h2>Can I export my log?</h2>
  <p>Yes. Use CSV export inside the app, then choose where to save or share the file.</p>

  <h2>Does the app give medical advice?</h2>
  <p>No. Back Pain Log is a diary and tracking tool. It does not diagnose, prescribe, or replace a qualified health professional.</p>

  <h2>Does the app collect analytics or tracking data?</h2>
  <p>No. Back Pain Log has no analytics, no advertising trackers, and no developer data collection. See our <a href="/back-pain-tracker/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for details.</p>

  <h2>Need more help?</h2>
  <p>Email us at <a href="mailto:support@mikhailnarbekov.com">support@mikhailnarbekov.com</a>. We aim to reply within a few business days.</p>
</LegalLayout>
